{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"command -v jq; command -v apply_patch; sed -n '1,180p' .codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md; sed -n '1,180p' global_memory_summary.md; ls -l global_memory/memory.md global_memory/memory.jsonl; sed -n '1,160p' source_evidence/downstream/program/program_spec.toml; sed -n '1,230p' source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"command -v jq; command -v apply_patch; sed -n '1,180p' .codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md; sed -n '1,180p' global_memory_summary.md; ls -l global_memory/memory.md global_memory/memory.jsonl; sed -n '1,160p' source_evidence/downstream/program/program_spec.toml; sed -n '1,230p' source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py\"","aggregated_output":"/usr/bin/jq\n---\nname: memory-log\ndescription: Maintain a continuous, append-only `./memory.md` log of discoveries, evaluations, failures, and next hypotheses during agent runs.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nKeep durable run memory so idea evolution and program evidence are never lost between steps.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- At run start to initialize memory.\n- After every meaningful step (`idea`, `edit`, `evaluate`, `verify`, `paper`, `draft`).\n- Immediately after every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair.\n\n# What to do\n1. Initialize `./memory.md` if missing with these section headers:\n- `# Memory Log`\n- `## Context`\n- `## Idea Discoveries`\n- `## Program Evaluations`\n- `## Failures / Regressions`\n- `## Next Hypotheses`\n2. Also initialize global files if missing:\n- `./global_memory/memory.md`\n- `./global_memory/memory.jsonl`\n3. Never delete or rewrite prior entries; append only.\n4. For each appended entry, include:\n- timestamp\n- step type\n- change/discovery summary\n- concrete evidence\n- next action\n5. After every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair, append a `Program Evaluations` entry that includes:\n- `program_<idx>`\n- `combined_score`\n- `correct`\n- rubric pass/fail summary\n- `next_recommendation`\n6. For regressions or failed rubrics, append one root-cause hypothesis under `Failures / Regressions`.\n7. Before exit, append final status (`rubric_pass`, `cap_reached`, or task-specific stop reason) and next hypothesis under `Next Hypotheses`.\n8. When command execution is unavailable, use read/edit/write tools to append directly\nto the required markdown and JSONL files. Preserve all existing content. When command\nexecution is available, prefer the helper for deterministic dual-write:\n- script: detect the active agent config directory first, then use `<that-dir>/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py`\n- command template:\n```bash\nMEMORY_HELPER=\"$(find ./.claude ./.codex ./.cursor ./.opencode ./.gemini ./.pi -path '*/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py' -print -quit 2>/dev/null)\"\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" \\\n  --global-memory-md \"./global_memory/memory.md\" \\\n  --global-memory-jsonl \"./global_memory/memory.jsonl\" \\\n  --event-json '{\"step\":\"evaluate\",\"scope\":\"attempt\",\"summary\":\"...\",\"evidence\":\"...\",\"next_action\":\"...\",\"attempt_id\":\"{{ATTEMPT_ID}}\",\"idea_id\":\"{{IDEA_ID}}\",\"program_id\":\"program_2\",\"metrics\":{\"combined_score\":2.54,\"correct\":true}}'\n```\n9. JSONL event schema (required keys):\n- `timestamp` (auto-filled if omitted)\n- `step` (`idea|edit|evaluate|verify|paper|draft|final|conclusions_skip`)\n- `scope` (`idea|attempt|paper|campaign`)\n- `summary`\n- `evidence`\n- `next_action`\n- optional: `idea_id`, `attempt_id`, `program_id`, `metrics`, `rubrics`, `tags`\n\n10. Update distilled conclusions (`conclusions.md`).\n**Purpose.** `conclusions.md` is a *forward-looking guide* for the next worker (or your future self in a later cycle). Its job is to help readers (a) focus their effort on directions you've found promising, and (b) avoid spending compute on directions you've already shown to be unpromising. Each sentence should either point at a lead worth pursuing or warn against a dead end, framed so a researcher who has not read your `memory.md` can still act on it. Avoid chronology, restate-of-results, and post-mortem narration — those belong in `memory.md`. Conclusions are the synthesis layer that makes other workers' next cycles more efficient.\n\n**When.** After every memory-append in the cycle (idea / edit / evaluate / verify / paper / final), evaluate whether `conclusions.md` should be updated.\n\n**Update gate (the only valid triggers).**\n- (a) cycle **contradicts** an existing sentence → rewrite that sentence.\n- (b) cycle opens a **new category** not yet covered → add a sentence.\n- (c) cycle **flips a Do/Don't** recommendation → flip it.\n- (d) cycle **meaningfully refines** an existing sentence — narrows the conditions under which a rule holds, broadens its applicability to a config it wasn't known to apply to, sharpens a tentative claim into a confident one, or adds a qualifier the prior phrasing didn't cover → edit the sentence to incorporate the refinement. Simple re-confirmation in the same regime is **not** sufficient; you must identify the refinement dimension (narrow / broaden / sharpen / qualify) in `--gate-reason`.\n- otherwise → **keep**, do not invoke the helper.\n\n**Format constraints.** Single paragraph. ≤300 words. No blank lines (`\\n\\n`). Avoid detailed numerical figures — use qualitative thresholds (e.g. \"low LR\", \"small batch\") instead of precise floats like `LR=0.205`.\n\n**Update mechanism.** When execution is unavailable, apply the same validation rules\nand update the conclusions files directly with read/edit/write tools. When execution\nis available, use this helper invocation:\n```bash\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" --write-conclusions \\\n  --conclusions-md \"{{CONCLUSIONS_MD_FILE}}\" \\\n  --conclusions-history-jsonl \"{{CONCLUSIONS_HISTORY_FILE}}\" \\\n  --cycle-index {{CYCLE_INDEX}} \\\n  --worker-index {{WORKER_INDEX}} \\\n  --gate-trigger <a|b|c|d> \\\n  --gate-reason \"<one sentence; for (d) name the dimension>\" \\\n  --conclusions-text \"<the full new paragraph>\"\n```\n\n**Pre-flight self-check.** Before invoking the helper, count words (`len(paragraph.split())`) and confirm ≤300, and that the paragraph contains no blank line. Most validation rejections can be avoided here.\n\n**Retry budget — exactly 3 attempts per cycle.** On non-zero exit, read the stderr error, shorten the paragraph (drop the least-decisive sentence, merge two related sentences, or remove qualifiers), and retry. After **3 total attempts** with no success, the update is **discarded** for this cycle: do not retry further, do not write the rejected text anywhere, and append a single memory event with `step=\"conclusions_skip\"` whose `summary` names the last validation error. Underlying findings are not lost — they are already durable in `memory.md`.\n\n**Always log the gate decision.** Inside the regular memory append for the cycle, include `gate=<updated|kept|skipped>; trigger=<a|b|c|d|none>; reason=<one sentence>` in the entry's `summary` or `tags`. Use `skipped` only after the 3-attempt budget is exhausted.\n\n# Example evaluation entry\n```markdown\n### 2026-02-13T16:58:00Z | step=evaluate\n- program: program_3\n- combined_score: 2.54\n- correct: true\n- rubrics: uses_restarts=pass, constraint_optimization=pass, score_threshold=fail\n- evidence: late-stage overlap still visible in stdout trace\n- next_recommendation: raise late-stage overlap penalty and diversify restart seeds\n```\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-17 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Certified Attainability Frontiers for Targeted Leaderboard Investment; wrote matching idea and rubric bundles. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Only an untested proposal and the supplied incumbent aggregate are available, so no evidence-backed distilled recommendation is added.\n  - evidence: Supplied bootstrap correct=true and combined_score=0.53012102014295; no recent ideas or attempts. Named external incumbent source was unavailable; implementation details and failure causes remain unknown. Alternatives were perfect-score-only attacks, unsupported training-cost curves, and a wider aggregation-rule catalogue. Bounded score-response ceilings permit exact support-cost certificates using documented public score matrices. No experiments or literature searches were run. Only canonical local memory path ideas/01_certified_attainability_frontiers_for_targeted_leaderboard_investment/memory.md was created for this idea.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-17T12:50:05.435064+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.42832805393112416, correct=False; scientific acceptance failed; cause unavailable; correct=false alone does not establish a protocol or implementation defect; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": 0.42832805393112416, \"control_pass_rate\": 0.9525462962962963, \"correct\": false, \"feasible_rate\": 0.4027777777777778, \"mean_effort_fraction\": 0.7963369070825209, \"mean_verified_gap_fraction\": 0.18981481481481483}\n- 2026-11-17 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Amortized Rank Window Certificates for Targeted Investment and wrote matching bundles. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=The proposal is untested, the recorded failure cause remains unavailable, and interface restrictions were already recorded rather than newly established scientific findings.\n  - evidence: Read named task/results/memory/skills and prior candidate source/spec. Interface supports uploaded matrices, mean/median/trimmed, common alpha, strict-first margin 1e-10, original-column outputs, work_seconds and node_budget. Prior source repeats whole-matrix aggregation per decision; amortization is a hypothesis, not a failure explanation. Prior combined_score=0.42832805393112416, correct=false, control_pass_rate=0.9525462962962963, feasible_rate=0.4027777777777778, mean_effort_fraction=0.7963369070825209, mean_verified_gap_fraction=0.18981481481481483; incumbent combined_score=0.53012102014295, correct=true. External incumbent source unavailable. Alternatives: repeated prefix-only certification, unsupported Borda/paper operations, and unobserved training costs. Selected conservative rank-window envelopes plus verified supports and shared preprocessing. No project code, tests, evaluator, literature search, or computational probes run. Canonical local target computed once after ID/title finalization: ideas/02_amortized_rank_window_certificates_for_targeted_investment/memory.md; no alternate same-cycle target created or used.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-17T13:06:05.197872+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.42913823911630933, correct=False; scientific acceptance failed; cause unavailable; correct=false alone does not establish a protocol or implementation defect; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": 0.42913823911630933, \"control_pass_rate\": 0.9552469135802469, \"correct\": false, \"feasible_rate\": 0.4027777777777778, \"mean_effort_fraction\": 0.7963369070825209, \"mean_verified_gap_fraction\": 0.18981481481481483}\n- 2026-11-17 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Coupled Clipped Score Certificates for Targeted Investment and wrote matching bundles. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=The proposed envelope has not been implemented or evaluated, and available acceptance feedback does not establish a failure cause or a validated change in practical recommendations.\n  - evidence: Read named workflows/task/histories/manifest/memory/conclusions and prior candidate source/spec. Prior combined scores 0.42832805393112416 and 0.42913823911630933 both had correct=false; effort, feasibility, and verified-gap aggregates were unchanged, with slightly different control_pass_rate. Incumbent combined_score=0.53012102014295, correct=true. Failure cause unknown. Alternatives were additional caching, repeated prefix certification, costly exhaustive large-panel search, and unsupported Borda/training/paper operations. Selected a minimax hinge envelope coupling retained ranks through one support budget; its practical benefit is untested. No program/evaluator execution, computational probes, package installation, or literature search occurred. Canonical local directory finalized once after ID/title: ideas/03_coupled_clipped_score_certificates_for_targeted_investment/memory.md; no alternate same-cycle target or staging memory was created or used.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-17T13:18:02.192017+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.42832805393112416, correct=False; scientific acceptance failed; cause unavailable; correct=false alone does not establish a protocol or implementation defect; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": 0.42832805393112416, \"control_pass_rate\": 0.9525462962962963, \"correct\": false, \"feasible_rate\": 0.4027777777777778, \"mean_effort_fraction\": 0.7963369070825209, \"mean_verified_gap_fraction\": 0.18981481481481483}\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 14227 Nov 17 13:18 global_memory/memory.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 14776 Nov 17 13:18 global_memory/memory.md\nschema_version = 1\ncode_root = \"src\"\n\n[entrypoint]\npath = \"program.py\"\nlanguage = \"python\"\ntype = \"script\"\n\n[copy]\nexclude = [\n  \"**/__pycache__/**\",\n  \"**/*.pyc\",\n  \".venv/**\",\n  \"node_modules/**\",\n  \".git/**\",\n  \".mypy_cache/**\",\n  \".pytest_cache/**\",\n  \".ruff_cache/**\",\n  \".tox/**\",\n  \".nox/**\",\n  \"dist/**\",\n  \"build/**\",\n]\ninclude = [\n]\n\n[integration]\nkind = \"generic\"\nnotes = \"\"\n\"\"\"Deterministic CPU counterfactual support solver, exposed only through handle.\n\nNative smoke copies this entrypoint only; keep source self-contained apart from\ninstalled packages. All requests/responses are finite JSON objects; additional response fields are\nforbidden. Each episode starts reset(seed: nonnegative integer), response\n{\"ok\": true}; any valid seed is supported and never chooses a workload. Reset\nclears uploaded values, results and all RNG state. No training is performed.\n\nupload accepts index (0-based integer), total (1..64), total_bytes (1..67108864),\nshape ([number of float64 values]), dtype=\"float64\", byte_order=\"little\",\nencoding=\"base64\", length (decoded bytes <=1048576), sha256 (chunk hex digest),\nand data (base64 string). Chunks must arrive in index order; upload index zero\nstarts candidate-owned in-memory transfer. Response: {\"ok\": true}. The logical\nvalue is concatenated little-endian float64 matrices, never a shared file.\n\nrun accepts matrices: list of {key: string, shape:[rows, columns], offset: byte\ninteger, task_ids: unique strings}, and decisions: list of {id: string,\nmatrix: key, target: row integer, columns: unique column integers, rule:\n\"mean\"|\"median\"|\"trimmed\", alpha: float in [0,1], node_budget: positive integer}.\nAt most 432 decisions, 10000 rows and 100 columns per matrix. Inputs are public\nscores in [0,1]; target and rivals are all visible. Only the target may change:\nx[j] becomes x[j]+alpha*(1-x[j]) on selected columns. Rivals are fixed. Columns\nlist the intervention/aggregation panel; selected indices are ORIGINAL matrix\ncolumn indices, not positions in that list. Strict first means aggregate exceeds\nall rivals by >1e-10. All tasks have equal weight; trimmed drops floor(0.2*m)\nvalues from EACH end; even median averages the two middle values. Task IDs have\nsemantic identity under joint permutations. Seeds are RNG initialization only.\nnode_budget is advisory; external wall and RPC limits are enforced independently.\nrun also accepts work_seconds: positive finite seconds remaining in the matched\nmethod reservation after uploads. It is plane-independent, excludes no transport\nor output cost, and is a snapshot, not an extension of the enforced deadline.\nSolvers may divide it across the supplied decisions and reserve output time;\nnever infer workload or evaluation identity from a seed.\n\nrun response is {\"chunks\": integer 1..16, \"total_bytes\": integer 1..16777216,\n\"sha256\": hex digest}. Results are UTF-8 JSON {\"plans\": list} in decision order.\nEach plan has EXACT keys id, selected (unique column integers), status\n(\"bounded\", \"optimal\", or \"infeasible\"), lower_bound (integer 0..m+1).\nNo candidate scores, internal state claims or diagnostics are accepted. Bounded\nplans can be non-winning, including empty, with conservative lower_bound=0;\nthis reports an unresolved interval, not infeasibility. Optimal claims need an\nindependently verifiable certificate: conservative full-panel reference bounds\nor exhaustive <=6-column audit. Infeasible means even all allowed uplifts cannot\nwin, uses selected=[] and lower_bound=m+1. Do not claim unverified exactness.\n\nread(index: output chunk integer) returns EXACT {index, encoding:\"base64\",\nlength: decoded byte integer <=1048576, sha256: hex digest, data: base64}.\nAll complete JSON messages, including framing, must be strictly below 64 MiB.\nrelease() clears transfer/results and returns {\"ok\":true}. No export/import of\nhidden solver state exists. Sequence: reset, 1..64 uploads, run, 1..16 reads,\nrelease. Maximum 83 calls per episode. There are no filesystem RPC fields.\n\nThis starter exhausts <=6-column panels, solves mean via sorted headroom, and\nuses deterministic marginal-score greedy for larger median/trimmed panels.\nThese are transparent reference choices, not claims of novel optimization or\nreal training effects. Improve the actual solver, not method-name aliases.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport hashlib\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport math\nimport random\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n_state = {}\nTOLERANCE = 1e-10\nCHUNK_BYTES = 1048576\n\n\ndef aggregate(values, rule):\n    if rule == \"mean\":\n        return float(np.mean(values))\n    ordered = np.sort(values)\n    if rule == \"median\":\n        return float(np.median(ordered))\n    trim = len(ordered) // 5\n    return float(np.mean(ordered[trim:len(ordered)-trim]))\n\n\ndef solve(matrix, task_ids, decision):\n    columns = decision[\"columns\"]\n    values = matrix[:, columns]\n    target = decision[\"target\"]\n    rule = decision[\"rule\"]\n    alpha = decision[\"alpha\"]\n    target_values = values[target].copy()\n    rival_values = np.delete(values, target, axis=0)\n    if rule == \"mean\":\n        rivals = np.mean(rival_values, axis=1)\n    elif rule == \"median\":\n        rivals = np.median(rival_values, axis=1)\n    else:\n        trim = values.shape[1] // 5\n        rivals = np.mean(np.sort(rival_values, axis=1)[:, trim:values.shape[1]-trim], axis=1)\n    threshold = float(np.max(rivals)) + TOLERANCE\n    def wins(selected):\n        updated = target_values.copy()\n        updated[selected] += alpha * (1-updated[selected])\n        return aggregate(updated, rule) > threshold\n    size = len(columns)\n    result = {\"id\": decision[\"id\"], \"selected\": [], \"status\": \"bounded\", \"lower_bound\": 0}\n    if not wins(list(range(size))):\n        result.update(status=\"infeasible\", lower_bound=size+1)\n        return result\n    ordered = sorted(range(size), key=lambda index: task_ids[columns[index]])\n    if size <= 6:\n        for count in range(size+1):\n            for selected in itertools.combinations(ordered, count):\n                if wins(list(selected)):\n                    result.update(selected=[columns[index] for index in selected], status=\"optimal\", lower_bound=count)\n                    return result\n    if rule == \"mean\":\n        order = sorted(range(size), key=lambda index: (-(1-target_values[index]), task_ids[columns[index]]))\n        selected = []\n        for index in order:\n            if wins(selected):\n                break\n            selected.append(index)\n        result.update(selected=[columns[index] for index in selected], status=\"optimal\", lower_bound=len(selected))\n        return result\n    selected = []\n    current = target_values.copy()\n    while not wins(selected):\n        available = [index for index in ordered if index not in selected]\n        def key(index):\n            trial = current.copy()\n            trial[index] += alpha * (1-trial[index])\n            return (-aggregate(trial, rule), task_ids[columns[index]])\n        index = min(available, key=key)\n        selected.append(index)\n        current[index] += alpha * (1-current[index])\n    result[\"selected\"] = [columns[index] for index in selected]\n    return result\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    operation = request[\"op\"]\n    if operation == \"reset\":\n        seed = request[\"seed\"]\n        if type(seed) is not int or seed < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid seed\")\n        _state.clear()\n        _state.update(seed=seed, chunks=[], output=None)\n        random.seed(seed)\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    if operation == \"upload\":\n        index, total = request[\"index\"], request[\"total\"]\n        if request[\"dtype\"] != \"float64\" or request[\"byte_order\"] != \"little\" or request[\"encoding\"] != \"base64\":\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid encoding\")\n        if not 1 <= total <= 64 or not 1 <= request[\"total_bytes\"] <= 64*CHUNK_BYTES:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid transfer bound\")\n        data = base64.b64decode(request[\"data\"], validate=True)\n        if len(data) != request[\"length\"] or len(data) > CHUNK_BYTES or hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest() != request[\"sha256\"]:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid chunk\")\n        if index == 0:\n            _state[\"chunks\"] = []\n            _state[\"transfer\"] = (total, request[\"total_bytes\"], request[\"shape\"])\n        if index != len(_state[\"chunks\"]) or _state[\"transfer\"] != (total, request[\"total_bytes\"], request[\"shape\"]):\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid chunk order\")\n        _state[\"chunks\"].append(data)\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    if operation == \"run\":\n        work_seconds = request[\"work_seconds\"]\n        if type(work_seconds) not in (int, float) or not math.isfinite(work_seconds) or work_seconds <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid work budget\")\n        total, total_bytes, shape = _state[\"transfer\"]\n        blob = b\"\".join(_state[\"chunks\"])\n        if len(_state[\"chunks\"]) != total or len(blob) != total_bytes or shape != [total_bytes//8] or total_bytes % 8:\n            raise ValueError(\"incomplete transfer\")\n        matrices = {}\n        for specification in request[\"matrices\"]:\n            rows, columns = specification[\"shape\"]\n            if not 2 <= rows <= 10000 or not 1 <= columns <= 100:\n                raise ValueError(\"invalid matrix dimensions\")\n            matrix = np.frombuffer(blob, dtype=\"<f8\", count=rows*columns, offset=specification[\"offset\"]).reshape(rows, columns)\n            if not np.all(np.isfinite(matrix)) or np.any(matrix < 0) or np.any(matrix > 1):\n                raise ValueError(\"invalid scores\")\n            matrices[specification[\"key\"]] = (matrix, specification[\"task_ids\"])\n        if not 1 <= len(request[\"decisions\"]) <= 432:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid decision count\")\n        plans = [solve(*matrices[decision[\"matrix\"]], decision) for decision in request[\"decisions\"]]\n        output = json.dumps({\"plans\": plans}, allow_nan=False, separators=(\",\", \":\")).encode()\n        if not 1 <= len(output) <= 16*CHUNK_BYTES:\n            raise ValueError(\"output too large\")\n        _state[\"output\"] = output\n        return {\"chunks\": math.ceil(len(output)/CHUNK_BYTES), \"total_bytes\": len(output), \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(output).hexdigest()}\n    if operation == \"read\":\n        index = request[\"index\"]\n        output = _state[\"output\"]\n        if type(index) is not int or not 0 <= index < math.ceil(len(output)/CHUNK_BYTES):\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid output index\")\n        data = output[index*CHUNK_BYTES:(index+1)*CHUNK_BYTES]\n        return {\"index\": index, \"encoding\": \"base64\", \"length\": len(data), \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(), \"data\": base64.b64encode(data).decode(\"ascii\")}\n    if operation == \"release\":\n        seed = _state[\"seed\"]\n        _state.clear()\n        _state[\"seed\"] = seed\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    raise ValueError(\"unknown operation\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
